<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Solapur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Solapur is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>. A fortified town held in turn by the Bahmani, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a> sultanates and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, it passed to the British in 1818. In the late 19th century it grew into a major centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> textile manufacture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solapur.jpg" alt="Solapur" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jadhavvv91 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solapur_Municipal_Corporation_building,_Indra_Bhuvan_credit_Alka_Kshirsagar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
